From a1d9f4e34e906fdc5af401b7908e5046aada7f32 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Junction 2026 team <junction2026@localhost>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 07:21:58 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] feat(backend): say when a remote trainer predates early
 stopping

A trainer built before early stopping validates the spec with
extra="forbid". With early stopping off nothing changes: the fields are
not sent. With it on, such a trainer refuses the job, and Studio used to
pass on the raw pydantic error ("early_stopping_patience: Extra inputs
are not permitted") or a bare 422.

explain_trainer_rejection() recognizes that rejection and the job fails
with "The remote trainer does not support early stopping: it runs
trainer code from before the feature existed. Redeploy or update the
trainer (for Modal: deploy the trainer again from this Studio), or train
without early stopping." This covers the remote trainer service (422 on
POST /jobs, before any upload), Modal and AWS Batch (failed status.json
from the batch worker, after the dataset upload). Other failures are
reported as before.

The tests rebuild the spec as it was before the feature to play the old
trainer. docs/remote-trainer.md describes the spec compatibility rule.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
